To address these complexities, organizations should consider adopting flexible management strategies that can be tailored to the specific needs of different teams or individuals, balancing the need for monitoring with the benefits of autonomy. This might involve implementing digital tools for self-reporting of progress, regular virtual check-ins, or outcome-based evaluations that focus on the quality and timeliness of work rather than the time spent on tasks. By doing so, organizations can better support the diverse needs of their workforce and potentially enhance overall productivity.

